# D-111 (steps/defects.md): the value of a `return:` in a method whose result is a Structure was admitted
# (l2_admit_return) and never checked as a value -- a call in it recorded no edge and met no rule of §14.
# `mk` declares Oops; `p` returns `mk()` and neither catches Oops nor lists it: refused at the return, as
# the same call is when the result is a number.  Before, the internal backstop at 1:1 alone.
Model:
    size_t: a 1U
end: Model
fn: mk () Model
    throws: Oops
    x: merge: Model
    throw: Oops()
    return: x
fn: p () Model
return: mk()

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
